  "camera_positions_note": "Camera positions and headings were placed with last year's greedy method for flight 10 m above ground, with buildings as walls and views cut where buildings block them, against three routes (north-east, south-east and south-west corners to the tower's north side).",
  "camera_height_above_ground_m": 14.0,
  "view_model": "Authoritative rule, use this one: a camera sees the attacker when (1) the attacker is within 30 deg either side of the camera heading, (2) within 150 m horizontally, and (3) the straight 3D line from the camera to the attacker does not pass through any building (vertical prisms: outline x [ground, ground + height_m]; the camera's own building counts). seen.py implements this rule. visible_area_enu_m in camera_schedule_10hz.jsonl is the area at flight height that each camera sees at each 0.1 s (arc drawn with 5 deg segments). Intrinsics and pitch are for rendering camera images only.",
  "obstacles": {
    "rule": "Every building in buildings_enu.json taller than 10 m (height_m) is a no-fly area; the attacker keeps vehicle_radius_m = 2 m clear of its outline. Lower buildings and everything else are open. There are no other obstacles.",
